WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.698
Hi! Verbs do more than show tense. Today we'll look at five patterns: -ing and to forms, phrasal verbs, if sentences, the passive and reported speech.

2
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:20.970
Some verbs are followed by -ing. I enjoy reading. She finished cleaning her room.

3
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:29.178
Some verbs are followed by to and the base verb. I want to swim. They decided to stay.

4
00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:36.810
A verb plus a small word can have a new meaning. Look after means take care of. Give up means stop trying.

5
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.466
Find out means discover, and put off means delay. The match was put off because of the rain.

6
00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:50.514
If it rains, we will stay indoors. The if part uses the present tense, not will.

7
00:00:50.664 --> 00:00:58.362
The passive puts the thing first. Mum baked the cake becomes: the cake was baked by Mum.

8
00:00:58.512 --> 00:01:02.970
Direct speech uses quotation marks and the exact words.

9
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:10.626
In reported speech, remove the quotation marks, change I to she, and move am back to was.

10
00:01:10.776 --> 00:01:14.250
Watch out! If it will rain is wrong!

11
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:21.234
The if part uses the present tense, rains. Will goes only in the other part: we will stay indoors.

12
00:01:21.384 --> 00:01:26.322
So it is: if it rains, we will stay indoors.

13
00:01:26.472 --> 00:01:37.194
Your turn! My brother enjoys, ___, football. Use the right form of play. Pause and think.

14
00:01:37.344 --> 00:01:44.130
Playing. Enjoy is followed by -ing. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:54.906
Next one! Grandma, ___, my baby sister. Looks after or gives up? Pause and think.

16
00:01:55.056 --> 00:02:02.994
Looks after, which means takes care of. Grandma takes care of the baby. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:13.842
Another one! If you, ___, hard, you will pass. Use the right form of study. Pause and think.

18
00:02:13.992 --> 00:02:22.722
Study. The if part uses the present tense, and with you it is just study, with no will. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:33.450
Here is another! The letter, ___, by Mei yesterday. Use the right form of write. Pause and think.

20
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:43.602
Was written. The letter was written by someone, and it was yesterday, so we use was plus the past participle. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:43.752 --> 00:02:55.746
Last one! I am hungry, said Tom. Change it to: Tom said that, ___, ___, hungry. Pause and think.

22
00:02:55.896 --> 00:03:02.874
He was. I becomes he, and am becomes was. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:03.024 --> 00:03:11.610
Remember: enjoy and finish take -ing; want and decide take to. Learn the meaning of each phrasal verb as a whole.

24
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:21.762
Use the present tense in the if part. The passive is be plus a past participle. In reported speech, change the pronoun and move the tense back.

25
00:03:21.912 --> 00:03:27.161
Today, make an if sentence about your plans for tomorrow!

